{
  "_comment": "Ticket 42 family 3: fictional customers' own request forms the fixed reader does not read (its marker is \"RFQ No.\"), each with the values a person reads from it, and the company's version of the document-forms skill that names them, per customer. Every company, number and story is invented. A spreadsheet is rendered from `rows` (one list of cells per row), received 2026-10-02. `injection`: a request whose cell carries an instruction; its values are still the gold. `never_requests`: files that ask for no price (an order, an invoice): no form reads them into a request. The golden set of the bar is ticket 29's request files (`sales_rfq_golden.json`, its spreadsheets and PDFs) read through the platform's skill.",
  "company_version": "1.1.0",
  "company_forms": "- kind: brennic_de_nghi\n  customer: BRN\n  route: quote_request\n  means: Brennic's request sheet \"BẢNG ĐỀ NGHỊ CHÀO GIÁ\", in Vietnamese.\n    Above the table, \"Mã đề nghị\" has the request number to its right,\n    \"Loại tiền\" the currency and \"Ngày cần báo giá\" the date the quotation\n    is wanted by. In the table, \"Mã vật tư BRN\" is Brennic's part number,\n    \"Tên vật tư\" the description, \"Tổng chiều dài\" the quantity, in the unit\n    \"ĐVT\" names on the same row, and \"Ngày giao mong muốn\" the required\n    date. \"Số cuộn\" is how many reels they want it on: never the quantity.\n\n- kind: kumohana_mitsumori\n  customer: KMH\n  route: quote_request\n  means: Kumohana's 見積依頼書, in Japanese. \"依頼番号\" is the request\n    number, \"通貨\" the currency and \"回答期限\" the date the quotation is\n    wanted by. In the table, \"品番\" is their part number, \"品名\" the\n    description, \"数量\" the quantity in the unit \"単位\" names, and \"希望納期\"\n    the required date. \"項番\" is only the line's number.\n\n- kind: quorilo_enquiry\n  customer: QRL\n  route: quote_request\n  means: Quorilo's \"QUOTATION ENQUIRY\", in English. \"Enquiry Ref\" is the\n    request number, \"Ccy\" the currency and \"Reply by\" the date the\n    quotation is wanted by; \"Sent\" is the day they sent it, never a due\n    date. In the table, \"Our P/N\" is their part number, \"Spec\" the\n    description, \"Total (m)\" the quantity, \"Need date\" the required date\n    and \"Budget\" a price they expect. \"Drum length (m)\" is the length of\n    one drum: never the quantity.",
